.combined_score\"\n141\t      ]\n142\t    },\n143\t    {\n144\t      \"citation_keys\": [],\n145\t      \"claim\": \"Derived: fitted multiplicative delay factor per width doubling is 0.980 (interval 0.557 to 1.425); over 16->256 it is 0.924 (interval 0.096 to 4.12); at the reference slope 0.230.\",\n146\t      \"source_ids\": [\n147\t        \"final.metric.grok_delay_log_slope\",\n148\t        \"final.metric.grok_delay_slope_ci_low\",\n149\t        \"final.metric.grok_delay_slope_ci_high\",\n150\t        \"final.metric.reference_delay_log_slope\"\n151\t      ]\n152\t    },\n153\t    {\n154\t      \"citation_keys\": [],\n155\t      \"claim\": \"Derived arithmetic from protocol constants (not from an evaluator metric): with delay floored at 250 and capped at 10,000 steps (ratio 40), OLS weights (-0.2,-0.1,0,0.1,0.2) over widths 16..256 give a maximum attainable |slope| of 0.3*ln(40)=1.107; a log-linear cap-to-floor profile gives 0.922.\",\n156\t      \"evidence_files\": [\n157\t        \"derived/resolution.json#max_abs_slope_attainable\",\n158\t        \"derived/resolution.json#loglinear_full_range_slope\",\n159\t        \"source_evidence/workload/final_manifest.json#full\",\n160\t        \"scripts/derive_resolution.py\"\n161\t      ],\n162\t      \"source_ids\": []\n163\t    },\n164\t    {\n165\t      \"citation_keys\": [],\n166\t      \"claim\": \"Derived: interval width 0.939, covering 42% of [-1.107,1.107]; arms 0.565 below and 0.374 above the point estimate.\",\n167\t      \"source_ids\": [\n168\t        \"final.metric.grok_delay_log_slope\",\n169\t        \"final.metric.grok_delay_slope_ci_low\",\n170\t        \"final.metric.grok_delay_slope_ci_high\"\n171\t      ]\n172\t    },\n173\t    {\n174\t      \"citation_keys\": [],\n175\t      \"claim\": \"Derived: a point estimate below -0.374 would have been needed for a 'supported' verdict with the same upper arm; the reference slope plus the same upper arm gives +0.006 (illustrative arithmetic).\",\n176\t      \"sou